<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corbinian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 670–730</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Saint Corbinian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Corbinian was a Frankish missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> who worked at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freising">Freising</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> around 720 and is regarded as the founder of its diocese. According to legend, a bear killed his pack horse on the road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and was made to carry his baggage, and the 'Corbinian bear' appears in the arms of Freising and of Pope Benedict XVI.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corbinian.jpg" alt="Corbinian" width="320" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Polack · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Corbinian_polack.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
